A||||4||Tom88gt||88 V-6 still won't start.  Ignition problem???||||8||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||01-15-2000||07:47 PM||||My Formula died the other day and I've been pulling my hair out trying to find out what's wrong.  I have fuel pressure.  Just no spark.<P>I'm not getting any spark at the plugs or from the end of the plug wires.  I removed the coil wire and held it to ground and got a good spark.  The distributor, module & pick-up were replaced (under warranty).  The cap, rotor & plugs are all less than a month old.  The coil checked good with an ohm meter.  The sparkplug wires are about 20K miles old.<P>The tack filter has not been replaced (I think I can get it at the local parts store, they have a listing for an RFI capacitor - $5.99).<P>The top of the block, below the distributor was hit with a pressure washer for a second or two.  No more elsewhere on the top of the engine.  The distributor stayed dry (but was replaced free anyway, warranty).  The car ran fine for about 20-30 min and then died and won't even fire when trying to start it.  <P>Is it possible I've shorted out the tach filter?  It tests at about 12,000 ohms.  Is this good or bad?  Haynes has no specs or mention of this device.<P>Help please!!!!  My car is stuck at McDonalds.||||reg||8
Z||000001||daved||01-15-2000||08:26 PM||||You can disconnect the filter if you like. It only goes to the tach.  In series (in & out) you should read 40 to 50k Ohms, with almost infinity to ground. As this is a small capacitor, you may see the Ohms vary(go higher) as the cap. charges up from small the meter voltage.  Anything else..replace it with original equipment type, NOT an RFI device, O/K.||||reg||1
Z||000002||David Gamache||01-15-2000||10:02 PM||||A lack of voltage can be a few things. From the more obvious like the battery,fuses, and fusable links to the coil, faulty plug wires,or a defective module. The other possibilities are a broken timing chain or a broken roll pin in the distributor gear. Too many times I have replaced a part and overlooked it as a possibility for a later problem just because the part was new. unfortunately it is easy to purchase a part that is defective.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||01-16-2000||04:18 AM||||Did you say that you are getting a good spark from the coil wire but not from any of the spark plug wires? Like the spark is getting "lost" as it goes thru the cap/rotor? <P>Is the spark from the coil good (blue) and seems frequent enough (not just firing randomly)?<P>Make sure the inside of the cap is dry and terminals aren't corroded.<P>Check for spark on ALL wires, if any are good then the bad ones could be bad wires.<P>One really wierd thing I've seen happen (since you seem to be getting into that realm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )... The rotor was broken and didn't spin with the dist. shaft. Looked OK when I took the cap off, but would just spin on the shaft.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||87 Steve GT||01-16-2000||09:16 AM||||will a tach filter cause all that??||||reg||5
